Let  $a, b, c$  be the roots to the cubic equation  $x^3 - a_1 x^2 + b_1x - 1 = 0$ . Since  $a_1 > b_1$ , this cubic has a positive root greater than  $1$ , say  $a$ .**<span style="color:#f00">Claim:**</span> For each positive integer  $n$ , we have 
\begin{align*}
a_n &= a^{2^n}+ b^{2^n} + c^{2^n} 
b_n &= a^{-2^n} + b^{-2^n} + c^{-2^n}.
\end{align*}

*Proof:* The base cases follow by Vieta. Check that 
\begin{align*}
a_n^2 - 2b_n &= a^{2^{n+1}}+b^{2^{n+1}} + c^{2^{n+1}} + 2\left(a^{2^n}b^{2^n}+b^{2^n}c^{2^n}+c^{2^n}a^{2^n} - (abc)^{2^n}\left(a^{-2^n}+b^{-2^n}+c^{-2^n}\right)\right)
&= a^{2^{n+1}}+b^{2^{n+1}}+c^{2^{n+1}} = a_{n+1}.
\end{align*} Swapping  $\left(a^n, a^{-n}\right)$  yields the analogous recurrence.  $\blacksquare$ Now, if the cubic has two nonreal roots, the magnitude of the two nonreal roots are less than  $1$ , so for sufficiently large  $n$ ,  $a_n$  grows as  $a^{2^n}$ , which increases. Otherwise, the quantities  $b^{2^n}$  and  $c^{2^n}$  are always positive and increasing when  $b, c < -1$ , so the sequence  $\{a_n\}$  increases too in that case.

