so modulo configuration issues (which I will not care about) this shows  $X = X'$  and hence  $P$  lies on  $O_BO_C$ . Now we claim  $P$  lies also on the radical axis of  $\omega_B$  and  $\omega_C$ . This is just a computation: by similar triangles we may compute that  $UO_B/UX = (r_C - r_B)/(r_C + r_B)$ , so by shooting lemma  $PU = (r_B + r_C)^2/(4U_X)$ , and so  $4PU \cdot O_BU = r_C^2 - r_B^2$ . But  $4PU \cdot O_BU = PO_C^2 - PO_B^2$ , so we are done.

