add(before); add(shift(3.2,0)*after);
[/asy]**<span style="color:red">Remark:</span>** This deletion argument can be thought of in some special cases even before the realization of Hall, in the case where  $\mathcal{M}$  has only one person (Pip). This amounts to saying that if one of Pip's arcs isn't liked by anybody, then that arc can be deleted and the induction carries through.

