We claim that the fixed radical center is the midpoint of  $BC$ , call it  $M$ .
Let  $D \equiv BP \cap (QPK)$  ,  $E \equiv CP \cap (QPK)$  and  $F \equiv XY \cap BC$ . Denote  $(QPK)$  and  $(ABC)$  as  $\alpha$  and  $\beta$  respectively.

<span style="color:#00f">**Claim**</span>:  $QXBFE$  and  $QYCDF$  are cyclic.
<span style="color:#f00">*Proof*</span>: As  $Q$  is the Miquel Point of the complete quadrilateral  $BXYCAF$ , the points  $Q,X,B,F$  are cyclic. Now, notice \[\angle QEX=\angle QEP=\angle QKP=\angle QBX\] which implies  $Q,E,X,B$  are cyclic. Similarly,  $QYCDF$  is cyclic as desired.  $\square$ Now, we use Linearity of POP and define  $f(A)=\text{Pow}_A(\alpha)-\text{Pow}_A(\beta)$ .
Then, it suffices to show \[f(M)=2BM^2=\frac{f(B)+f(C)}{2}=\frac{CP \cdot CE-BP \cdot BD}{2} \iff CP \cdot CE-BP \cdot BE=BC^2.\]
We know  $CX \cdot CE=CB \cdot CF$  and  $BY \cdot BD=BC \cdot BF$ . Hence, it suffices to show \[\frac{CP \cdot CE-BP \cdot BD}{BC}=\frac{CP \cdot CE}{BC}-\frac{BP \cdot BD}{BC}=\frac{CP \cdot CF}{CX}-\frac{BP \cdot BF}{BY}=CF-BF.\] Simplifying this, it suffices to show \[\frac{CF \cdot XP}{CX}=\frac{BF \cdot PY}{BY} \iff \frac{BF}{FC} \cdot \frac{CX}{XP} \cdot \frac{PY}{YB}=1.\]This is clearly true by Menelaus Theorem in  $\triangle PBC$  with transversal  $\overline{FXY}$ . Hence,  $\text{Pow}_M(\alpha)=-\text{Pow}_M(\beta)=BM^2$  for all circles  $\alpha$  as described, which was to be shown.  $\blacksquare$

