This is a nice problem but way too easy for P8. Here is my solution.

Since  $x^{256}\equiv y^{256}\pmod{257}$  but  $x
ot\equiv y\pmod{257}$ , we take the maximal  $k$  such that  $x^{2^k}
ot\equiv y^{2^k}\pmod{257}$ . By maximality,   $$ 257\mid x^{2^{k+1}} - y^{2^{k+1}} = (x^{2^k}+y^{2^k})(x^{2^k}-y^{2^k}) $$  thus  $257\mid x^{2^k}+y^{2^k}$ . Manually check that  $x^{2^k}+y^{2^k}
e 257$ , so we are done.

