<details><summary>My solution</summary>To ease our pain, consider the simple case where the tree is a path of length \(n\).
<details><summary>Case: paths of length n</summary>Two automorphisms \(f : P_n \rightarrow P_n\) can happen:
The identity automorphism sends everything to itself, covering the first case \(\exists a. \quad f(a) = a\)
[asy]
