Let  $H'$  be the  orthocenter of  $\triangle APQ$ .
Then it is well known that  $H'F \bot AF$ .  $\Rightarrow H'$  lies on the line through  $F$  that is perpendicular to  $AB \Rightarrow H'$  lies on  $CF$ .

And, If  $D$  is the projection of  $A$  onto  $BC$ , then  $H'$  lies on  $AD$  also  $\Rightarrow$   $H' = AD \cap CF$   $\Rightarrow$   $H' = H$ Thus,  $H$  is also the orthocenter of  $\triangle APQ$ .

Now, Let  $A'$  be the antipode of  $A$  in  $(APQ)$ .
Then it is well known that  $A'$ ,  $B$ ,  $H$  are collinear  $\Rightarrow \angle A'EA = 90^{\circ} = \angle A'PA \Rightarrow E$  lies on  $(APQ)$ .

Also,  $\angle PEA = 180^{\circ} - \angle PQA = 180^{\circ} - \angle PQF - \angle FQA = 180^{\circ} - \angle FAQ - \angle FQA = \angle QFA$  

Now, Let  $QF \cap PE = T$ , then  $\angle AET= \angle PEA = \angle QFA = 180^{\circ} - \angle AFT \Rightarrow T$  lies on  $(AQP)$ .

Q.E.D.

