Now  $\sum_{k=1}^{n} \lambda_k (\sum_{l=1}^{k} x_l =(\sum_{k=1}^{n}\lambda_k)x_1+ ... +\lambda_n x_n$  and  $\varphi 0=0$ , then  $(\sum_{k=1}^{n}\lambda_k)x_1+ ... +\lambda_n x_n=0$ therefore,  $(\sum_{k=1}^{n}\lambda_k)=\alpha \lambda_1$ ,  $(\sum_{k=2}^{n}\lambda_k)=\alpha \lambda_2$ ,..., $\lambda_n=\alpha \lambda_n$ , where  $\alpha \neq 0 \in R$ i.e.  $\lambda_1=\lambda_2=...=\lambda_n=0$ So,  $x_1,x_2, ... ,x_n$  are linearly independent.

