Putting these two together,   $$ a_1 \equiv a_ka_{k-1}\cdots a_1\equiv a_2 \implies a_1\equiv a_2 $$  , but this is impossible since  $a_1,a_2\in \{1,2,\cdots,n\}$ . Thus, it is a contradiction and in-fact,  $n$  does not divide  $a_k(a_1-1)$  .

