Since  $\triangle QPB\sim \triangle MPK,$  we have that  $\dfrac{MK}{QB}=\dfrac{MP}{QP}=\dfrac{1}{2},$  so  $MK=\dfrac{QB}{2},$  and since  $\triangle CQP\sim \triangle LQM,$  we have that  $\dfrac{ML}{CP}=\dfrac{QM}{QP}=\dfrac{1}{2},$  so  $ML=\dfrac{CP}{2}.$  Now, since  $\triangle AQP\sim \triangle MLK,$  we have  $\dfrac{MK}{AP}=\dfrac{ML}{AQ},$  so  $\dfrac{AQ}{AP}=\dfrac{ML}{MK}=\dfrac{\left(\dfrac{CP}{2}\right)}{\left(\dfrac{QB}{2}\right)}=\dfrac{CP}{QB},$  so  $AQ\cdot QB=AP\cdot PC.$  

