Let the incircle touch  $\overline{BC}$  at  $X$  and the  $A$ -excircle  $\omega_A$  touch  $\overline{BC}$  at  $X'$  and  $\overline{AC}$  at  $Y'$ . Denote by  $\omega_R$  and  $\omega_S$  the circles centered at  $R$  and  $S$  respectively with radius  $0$ .

Note that  $BR=CY=CX=BX'$  and  $YR=BC=AY'-AY=YY'$ , so  $\overline{BY}$  is the radical axis of  $\omega_A$  and  $\omega_R$ . Similarly  $\overline{CZ}$  is the radical axis of  $\omega_A$  and  $\omega_S$ , so  $G$  is the radical center of  $\omega_A$ ,  $\omega_R$ ,  $\omega_S$  and therefore equidistant from  $R$  and  $S$ .

We use bary wrt  $ABC$ . Let  $x=s-a,y=s-b,z=s-c$ . Then  $G=(1/x : 1/y : 1/z)$ , so  $Z = (1/x:1/y:0)= \left(\frac{y}{x+y},\frac{x}{x+y},0\right)$ . Now,  $S=C+Z-B = \left(\frac{y}{x+y}, -\frac{y}{x+y}, 1\right)$ . Normalizing  $G$ , we get  $G = \left(\frac{yz}{N}, \frac{xz}{N}, \frac{xy}{N}\right)$ , where  $N=xy+yz+zx$ . The displacement vector  $\overleftrightarrow{GS}$  is then
\begin{align*}
\overleftrightarrow{GS} &= \left( \frac{y}{x+y} - \frac{yz}{N}, -\frac{y}{x+y}- \frac{xz}{N},  1-\frac{xy}{N} \right) 
&= \left( \frac{xy^2}{(x+y)N}, \ -\frac{xz(x+y)+yN}{(x+y)N}, \ \frac{(x+y)z}{N}\right)
\end{align*}
after some simplification. Since  $a=y+z,b=z+x,c=x+y$ , we then have
\begin{align*}
GS^2 &= (y+z)^2 \left( \frac{xz(x+y)+yN}{(x+y)N} \cdot \frac{(x+y)z}{N} \right) - (z+x)^2 \left(\frac{xy^2}{(x+y)N} \cdot \frac{(x+y)z}{N} \right) 
&\qquad + (x+y)^2  \left(\frac{xy^2}{(x+y)N} \cdot \frac{xz(x+y)+yN}{(x+y)N} \right) 
&= \frac{(y+z)^2z(xz(x+y)+yN) - (z+x)^2xy^2z+ xy^2(xz(x+y)+yN)}{N^2} 
&= \frac{x^2 y^4 + 2 x^2 y^3 z - x^2 y^2 z^2 + 2 x^2 y z^3 + x^2 z^4 + 2 x y^4 z + 4 x y^3 z^2 + 4 x y^2 z^3 + 2 x y z^4 + y^4 z^2 + 2 y^3 z^3 + y^2 z^4}{N^2} 
&= \frac{x^2(y^4+2y^3z-y^2z^2+2yz^3 + z^4) + x(2y^4z + 4y^3z^2 + 4y^2z^3 + 2yz^4) + (y^4z^2+2y^3z^3+y^2z^4)}{N^2},
\end{align*}
which is symmetric in  $y,z$ . Hence  $GR=GS$ .

