        AB+CD&=BC+DA,
        AB+CE&=BC+EA.
    \end{align*}
    Subtracting and rearranging, \[CD+EA=DA+CE,\]
    so  $ADCE$  is tangential, and  $E$  is the insimilicenter of  $\omega_1$ , and  $\omega_3$ , as desired.  $\blacksquare$ **Claim 2.**      $C$  lies on  $(I_1I_2I_3)$ .

