Note that  $I$  is the orthocenter of  $HBC$ . By the right angles on intouch chord lemma, if  $H_B = \overline{BI} \cap \overline{EF}$ , we have  $\angle BH_BC = 90^\circ$ , and if  $H_C$  is similarly defined, we have  $\angle BH_CC = 90^\circ$  as well. Hence, by Ceva/Menelaus Configuration  $(H, I; \overline{HD} \cap \overline{EF}, D) = -1$ . Meanwhile, noting that  $\overline{AKI} \parallel \overline{DM}$ , we have
\begin{align*}
